{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>It is the plague of tzara'at.</b> Scripture sometimes says נֶגַע צָרַעַת הוּא, sometimes צָרַעַת הִיא, sometimes צָרַעַת נוֹשֶׁנֶת הוּא, and sometimes נֶגַע הוּא — for tzara'at truly has, like other diseases, stages of onset, increase, and culmination, and if the ailment heals there is also a decline. He called the onset נֶגַע alone, the increase נֶגַע צָרַעַת, the culmination צָרַעַת; when it becomes chronic it is called צָרַעַת נוֹשֶׁנֶת, and when it is in decline he says נִרְפָּא הַנֶּגַע, נִרְפָּא הַנֶּתֶק. And since this kind of ailment serves as punishment, as they said of blessed memory: 'It is nothing but an altar of atonement' (Berakhot 5b), He appointed the periods of isolation in order to arouse [the person] toward repentance, as it says: וַיִּגֶל אָזְנָם לַמּוּסָר וַיֹּאמֶר כִּי יְשֻׁבוּן מֵאָוֶן (Job 36:10)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:37.691873310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}